cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ICS Deception Framework"
message: >-
  If you use this software in your research, please cite it using the
  metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "ICS Deception Framework contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/OWNER/ICS-Deception-Framework"
url: "https://github.com/OWNER/ICS-Deception-Framework"
abstract: >-
  A lightweight, distributed Industrial Control System deception and telemetry
  framework for authorized laboratory research. It provides a Modbus/TCP
  honeypot, a DNP3-inspired interaction sensor, interactive Telnet and
  SSH-banner decoys, a fake PLC node for Raspberry Pi class hardware, a
  loopback-bound FastAPI controller, structured JSONL event logging, and
  streaming PCAP analysis with controlled replay. An optional post-quantum
  evidence layer seals honeypot logs with ML-DSA-65 (FIPS 204) signatures
  over a SHA3-256 hash chain, making modification, deletion, reordering,
  duplication and replay of recorded events detectable, with optional
  ML-KEM-768 encrypted offline archives. The protocol services implement
  deliberately incomplete subsets of their protocols for deception purposes
  and are not standards-compliant implementations. The evidence layer is a
  tamper-evident technical mechanism and makes no claim regarding legal
  chain of custody.
keywords:
  - industrial control systems
  - SCADA
  - honeypot
  - deception technology
  - Modbus
  - DNP3
  - IoT security
  - security research
  - post-quantum cryptography
  - ML-DSA
  - FIPS 204
  - tamper-evident logging
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.3.0b1
date-released: "2026-08-05"

